   "shows": "One neuromuscular junction close up as a cut-away: a glass nerve bouton with vesicles, active zones, mitochondria and Schwann cell; the synaptic cleft with basement membrane, laminin, collagen IV and Q, acetylcholinesterase and agrin; the muscle side with six junctional folds, 1,677 acetylcholine receptors, MuSK/LRP4 and sodium channels; and the inside of the fibre with nuclei, ER, Golgi, myofibrils, desmin and plectin. Endotype clouds of genes can arrive and settle at their place.",
   "frame": "Up (+y) is the nerve, down the muscle. Cut plane z = 0.34 facing +z. Axon reaches up and left to about (-2.9, 2.3); the fibre's surface spreads to x +-5 for the wide view.",
   "size": "~2.4 across (x -1.2 to 1.2); 1 micrometre ~ 0.5 units; small parts drawn bigger than life",
